1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,508
In Indonesia, a small fault on a motorbike or a water pump can cost a day's wage, or days without water. Repair videos online are not for your model, not in your language, and they can't see your problem.

2
00:00:12,508 --> 00:00:23,456
Tukang Copilot turns any phone into a mechanic's apprentice. Take a photo and say what's wrong. This recording runs in demo mode, with labelled stand-in photos.

3
00:00:23,456 --> 00:00:31,140
Muse Voice Transcribe hears the problem, Muse Spark looks at the photo, and SAM 3.1 finds the exact parts.

4
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:36,760
When the evidence is ambiguous, it asks one short question instead of guessing.

5
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:45,788
Then the diagnosis: likely causes with confidence, a safety level, tools, time, and the parts cost against the repair-shop price.

6
00:00:45,788 --> 00:00:52,200
The parts are masked and numbered on your own photo by SAM 3.1, not a generic diagram.

7
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:58,468
Before step one, a short safety checklist. The steps stay locked until you tick every item.

8
00:00:58,468 --> 00:01:12,152
New: the live camera guide. Point the phone and SAM 3.1 outlines the exact part to touch, about once a second, on the live picture. In this demo the camera is Chromium's fake camera playing a stand-in photo.

9
00:01:12,152 --> 00:01:21,396
After each step, Check my step. Muse Spark compares the photo with the expected state. Too dark here, so it asks for the torch instead of guessing.

10
00:01:21,396 --> 00:01:25,396
Retake it, and the step is verified before you move on.

11
00:01:25,396 --> 00:01:38,384
Your hands are dirty, so go hands-free. Each step is read aloud and the phone listens for lanjut, ulang, cek or berhenti. Phones without continuous listening get push-to-talk through Voice Transcribe.

12
00:01:38,384 --> 00:01:47,124
Still broken? Say what happened, and the agent re-plans to the next most likely cause. Plan, act, verify, re-plan.

13
00:01:47,124 --> 00:01:57,784
And when it's a job for a pro, one tap hands it off: a WhatsApp summary of what was found and tried, a search for the nearest bengkel, and a PDF with a brief for the mechanic.

14
00:01:57,784 --> 00:02:06,812
It also knows when to say no. A rice cooker that won't heat would mean opening 220 volt internals, so the safety gate stops the guidance.

15
00:02:06,812 --> 00:02:12,840
The stop still gives you a PDF report and the hand-off card, so you're never left at a dead end.

16
00:02:12,840 --> 00:02:19,468
The whole app runs in Bahasa Indonesia, Javanese and English, with Javanese voice input.

17
00:02:19,468 --> 00:02:29,024
And with one switch, diagnosis and planning run on Muse Spark Open, Meta's open-weights model, on Baseten. The app shows a badge when it does.

18
00:02:29,024 --> 00:02:45,132
Under the hood: Voice Transcribe, Muse Spark for vision, diagnosis, planning and verification, SAM 3.1 for masks and live tracking, and Muse Image for diagrams your photo can't show. The safety gate is enforced in code, in three layers.

19
00:02:45,132 --> 00:02:50,132
Tukang Copilot. Every phone becomes a mechanic's apprentice.
